1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,348
Mara writes, “If this mattered to you, you would have shown up.”

2
00:00:04,348 --> 00:00:08,697
You fire back, “You have no idea what I was carrying.”

3
00:00:08,697 --> 00:00:10,325
Your thumb reaches Send.

4
00:00:10,325 --> 00:00:13,046
This is the second Selah is built for.

5
00:00:13,046 --> 00:00:16,041
It isn’t another Bible app you have to remember to open.

6
00:00:16,041 --> 00:00:19,427
It is a private pause, right where the argument is happening.

7
00:00:19,427 --> 00:00:20,703
Tap Pause.

8
00:00:20,703 --> 00:00:23,945
First, Gloo reads the heat—not who is right.

9
00:00:23,945 --> 00:00:27,630
Here it sees defensiveness, and a need to be understood.

10
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:30,091
That selects an allowlisted theme.

11
00:00:30,091 --> 00:00:34,283
YouVersion returns the exact passage and its wider context.

12
00:00:34,283 --> 00:00:37,330
The model never chooses or invents Scripture.

13
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:40,091
Then Selah asks one private question.

14
00:00:40,091 --> 00:00:43,554
It never writes the reply, and it never posts for you.

15
00:00:43,554 --> 00:00:45,273
Edit in your own words.

16
00:00:45,273 --> 00:00:46,927
Wait ten minutes.

17
00:00:46,927 --> 00:00:48,476
Or send anyway.

18
00:00:48,476 --> 00:00:51,250
Your voice—and your choice—stay yours.

19
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,057
And if the message is more than angry, Selah does not answer a crisis with a verse.

20
00:00:57,057 --> 00:00:58,255
It stops.

21
00:00:58,255 --> 00:00:59,986
No Scripture retrieval.

22
00:00:59,986 --> 00:01:01,406
No reflection.

23
00:01:01,406 --> 00:01:03,867
It points toward immediate human help.

24
00:01:03,867 --> 00:01:15,195
Underneath, every stage is bounded, schema-checked, and fail-closed: Gloo classifies, YouVersion retrieves, and Gloo reflects using only the returned text.

25
00:01:15,195 --> 00:01:18,151
Selah doesn’t ask technology to speak for you.

26
00:01:18,151 --> 00:01:23,815
It gives you one quiet moment to decide who you want to be—before your words leave your hands.

